<title>SPAIN: Spain's ICO gets 50 bln pta syndicated loan.</title>
<headline>Spain's ICO gets 50 bln pta syndicated loan.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spain's Official Credit Institute (ICO) received a syndicated loans from 32 financial entities for 50 billion pesetas over ten years, a statement said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Lead manager was the association of savings banks, CECA.</p>
<p>The loan has a fixed yield with a zero coupon.</p>
<p>ICO has been given the option from the first year to change the loan to a floating rate, at MIBOR plus 0.4 points.</p>
<p>-- Madrid Newsroom, + 341 585 8340</p>
</text>
